{
  "id": "inlay_hints/designator_hints/01_fields_and_indices",
  "topic": "inlay_hints",
  "subtopic": "designator_hints",
  "title": "Field and index designators",
  "summary": "Positional aggregate initialization shows `.field=`, and `[index]=` once enabled",
  "prose": "Array indices are off by default, `inlay_hints.array_indices` turns them on: a table would carry one on every element. Without them a path through an array shows its fields alone; with indices but no field designators it shows nothing. Array designators survive members whose size depends on a template parameter, and reserved member names are skipped rather than printed.",
  "status": "supported",
  "issues": [
    "clangd#1277"
  ],
  "files": [
    {
      "path": "main.cpp",
      "text": "struct Point {\n    int x;\n    int y;\n    int z;\n};\n\nPoint p{1, 2 + 2};\n\nint coordinates[2] = {7, 8};\n\ntemplate <typename T, int N>\nstruct Array {\n    T __elements[N];\n};\n\nArray<int, 2> pair = {0, 1};\n\nPoint corners[2] = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6};\n",
      "markers": []
    }
  ],
